# The SHA-1 of the certificate every macOS release binary must be signed with.
# Read by scripts/lib/mac-signing.sh (mac_pinned_sha1): '#' comments and blank
# lines are ignored, and what remains must be empty or exactly one 40-hex-digit
# fingerprint (colons, spaces and case do not matter).
#
# Pinned: "oam Code Signing (self-signed)", O=Yaw Labs, valid to 2048-08-28,
# generated on the build Mac with scripts/provision-mac-signing.sh --generate
# and backed up off that host. Signing with exactly this certificate is
# mandatory: a mac leg that cannot use it fails the release. (While this file
# held no fingerprint, the mac leg signed AD-HOC and warned.)
#
# Rotating it (a new identity, or the Developer ID) is the same edit: provision
# the new identity (streamed: ssh <mac> 'bash -s -- --generate' <
# scripts/provision-mac-signing.sh), back it up, and replace the line below.
5186628807511f9c1b81fd87bbfe0b2c02b0c647
